helpMsg:
An interactive terminal (REPL): ending the script with &quot;LIA: terminal&quot; opens an input line below the output after execution. send.handle(&quot;input&quot;, callback) is called for every line the user sends, send.handle(&quot;stop&quot;, callback) when the user stops the execution.

Example:
  ```js
  // execute me and type 2+2 into the terminal
  ```
  &lt;script&gt;
    send.handle(&quot;input&quot;, (input) =&gt; send.lia(String(eval(input))))
    &quot;LIA: terminal&quot;
  &lt;/script&gt;

replace:
```${1:js}
${2:// type JavaScript into the terminal after executing this block}
```
<script>
  send.handle("input", (input) => {
    ${3:send.lia(String(eval(input)))}
  })
  send.handle("stop", (e) => {
    ${4:console.log("stopped")}
  })
  "LIA: terminal"
</script>

